A||||5||Stenny||Valve train noise
Z||000000||Stenny||07-27-99||11:38 PM||||I have an 85 2m4 and I have started hearing ticking noises from under the valve cover. It sounds like I need a valve adjustment, but I know they're hydraulic. Do I need new lifters or is some adjustment possible? Thanks for any help!! Stenny
Z||000001||JetroGT||07-28-99||01:24 AM||||Is the ticking loud? When I had my 2M4 I had some sort of ticking that I thought was the lifters or loose valves, it turned out to be the cam gear.
Z||000002||batboy||07-28-99||05:54 AM||||Even with hydraulic lifters, there is some amount of adjustment that can be done at the rocker arm. Don't tighten them too much or the valve won't close all the way, which is bad.
Z||000003||ChadMan||07-28-99||07:07 AM||||The valvetrain on the Iron Duke is pretty clattery by nature, I think.  Try tightening down your valve cover bolts (but not too tight or you'll warp the cover!).  Mine was leaking like crazy, and when I tightened them down, it quieted down a lot of the ticking and clattering.
Z||000004||theogre||07-28-99||07:56 AM||||change the oil. If it's noise caused by a lame lifter that will often change the tune or eliminate it for a while.<p>If you get some oil stoppers you can find a loose rocker real fast. You pull the cover, put the stoppers on the rockers (they plug the oil hole so you don't drown the whole thing in oil) and start the car. Push down on each rocker with a stick. the loose one will shutup as soon as you push on it.
Z||000005||Stenny||07-28-99||08:22 AM||||I'll try to see if I have a loose rocker. It has fresh oil in it since I just put in rod bearings. I'll give it a try! Thanks!
